Private Function TemporaryMateMove(ByVal path As String, ByVal start As Object, ByVal shiftText As String, ByVal wanted As Variant, ByVal boxBefore As Variant, ByVal shiftX As Double, ByVal shiftY As Double, ByVal shiftZ As Double, ByVal kept As Object, ByRef text As String) As Boolean
    ' A24 flexible-move-temporary-mate: the part is moved by a Concentric mate (IAssemblyDoc.AddMate5, swMateCONCENTRIC) between its cylindrical face, taken in the top
    ' assembly's context (the selected handle of the drag operator's rung, else one selected here, else start; IComponent2.GetCorrespondingEntity), and a reference axis
    ' through the wanted place along the cylinder's axis. Read through a part found again (MoveRead); the mate, the axis and the 3D sketch are then deleted, the assembly is
    ' rebuilt and the part must STILL be at the wanted place (it is free in X and Y). The MateGroup's mates and the tree's features are recorded before and compared after
    ' EVERY path: whatever the rung left behind stops the recipe (a later rung must never run on, or the assembly be saved with, a stray mate, axis or sketch). True when the
    ' part moved; False leaves the part where it was and the next rung is tried; a part that goes back when the mate is deleted raises. On 2021, 2023 and 2026
